// The hand-off funnels reach six positions, not just an initializer. ARGUMENT and RETURN are the two
// that carry a value across a function boundary, where the declared type is the only thing a caller can
// read — so a crossing there is the one least likely to be noticed.
//
// Both errors are expected; the fixture asserts the rule is wired at `rejectValueKindMismatch` (argument
// + return + assignment) and not only at `rejectInitKindMismatch`.
type enum A : uint8 { A0, A1, A2 }
type enum B : uint8 { B0, B1, B2 }

fn void takeB(B b) { }

fn B asB(A a) { return a; }

fn int32 main()
{
    A a = A::A2;
    takeB(b: a);
    return 0;
}
